    <string name="welcome_title">welcome ku ylih</string>
    <string name="welcome_intro">ylih rekɔrdi hɔ́w lɔ́ng each pair ɔf headphɔnes stays cɔnnected, sɔ that years frɔm nɔw yɔu can still answer the ɔnly questiɔn that matters abɔut a pair: hɔw many hɔurs did they last?</string>
    <string name="welcome_point_auto_title">cɔnnect and fɔrget</string>
    <string name="welcome_point_auto_body">bluetɔɔth headphɔnes are recɔrded ɔn their ɔwn, frɔm the mɔment they cɔnnect. nɔthing has tɔ be left running.</string>
    <string name="welcome_point_lifetime_title">ɔne pair, ɔne lifetime</string>
    <string name="welcome_point_lifetime_body">when a pair dies, retire it: its tɔtal freezes there and the next pair ɔf the same headphɔnes starts again frɔm zerɔ.</string>
    <string name="welcome_point_detailed_title">wired and playback</string>
    <string name="welcome_point_detailed_body">detailed tracking, in settings, adds wired headphɔnes and measures hɔw much ɔf the time was actually playing.</string>
    <string name="welcome_privacy">everything stays ɔn this phɔne. there is nɔ accɔunt, and the app has nɔ internet permissiɔn.</string>
    <string name="welcome_start">get started</string>
    <string name="welcome_next">next</string>
    <string name="welcome_allow">allɔw</string>
    <string name="welcome_step">step %1$d ɔf %2$d</string>
    <string name="welcome_bluetooth_title">bluetɔɔth access</string>
    <string name="welcome_bluetooth_why">andrɔid ɔnly tells an app which bluetɔɔth device cɔnnected, and what it is called, if the app hɔlds bluetɔɔth access. it is hɔw ylih tells a pair ɔf headphɔnes frɔm a car stereo, and hɔw it knɔws ɔne pair frɔm anɔther.</string>
    <string name="welcome_bluetooth_with">with it: every pair is recɔrded frɔm the mɔment it cɔnnects, with nɔthing left running and nɔthing tɔ remember tɔ press.</string>
    <string name="welcome_bluetooth_without">withɔut it: nɔ bluetɔɔth headphɔnes are recɔrded at all. the rest ɔf the app still wɔrks, and yɔu can grant it later in andrɔid’s app settings.</string>
    <string name="welcome_notifications_title">nɔtificatiɔns</string>
    <string name="welcome_notifications_why">detailed tracking runs a small backgrɔund service, and andrɔid requires any app dɔing that tɔ keep a nɔtificatiɔn visible while it dɔes.</string>
    <string name="welcome_notifications_with">with it: the nɔtificatiɔn shɔws what is being recɔrded right nɔw, which is the ɔnly sign detailed tracking is alive.</string>
    <string name="welcome_notifications_without">withɔut it: detailed tracking still runs and still recɔrds. andrɔid just will nɔt shɔw its nɔtificatiɔn.</string>
    <string name="hibernation_title">keep cɔunting while yɔu fɔrget abɔut it</string>
    <string name="hibernation_body">andrɔid pauses apps that gɔ unɔpened fɔr a few mɔnths and takes their permissiɔns back, which wɔuld leave ylih recɔrding nɔthing until yɔu next ɔpened it. being fɔrgɔtten abɔut is exactly what this app is fɔr, sɔ it is wɔrth turning that ɔff nɔw.</string>
    <string name="action_not_now">nɔt nɔw</string>

